<!doctype html><html lang="en-CA"><head><meta charset="utf-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1"/><title>Index | PictureThis Production</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap"/></head><body><a href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="masthead"><a href="/"><b>PICTURETHIS PRODUCTION</b></a><nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="/">Home</a><a href="/programs/">Programs</a><a href="/faithfire/">Faithfire</a><a href="/projects/">Projects</a><a href="/blog/">Blog</a><a href="/events/">Events</a><a href="/partners/">Partners</a><a class="nav-action" href="/get-involved/">Get Involved</a><a href="/donate/">Donate</a></nav></header><main id="main"><section class="page-opening"><figure class="production-photo"><img src="https://doop.design/photos/pexels/8412361.jpeg?h=900&w=1600" alt="Two camera operators working beside production cameras" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Illustrative photography</figcaption></figure><h2>Cohort One — the Faithfire story</h2><p>The first cohort wasn't a class. It was a crew. Faithfire Production is where PictureThis got its start: a church production team at 139 Millwick Dr that grew into a full production department, one show at a time. Most of the crew started with little to no experience. They learned the way this program teaches today: by shadowing someone more experienced, helping out on real shows, and then running their own positions.</p><figure class="production-photo"><img src="https://doop.design/photos/pexels/11410604.jpeg?h=900&w=1600" alt="Production crew preparing equipment backstage" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Illustrative photography</figcaption></figure><p>These days, that crew handles two Sunday services plus events like Cue & A and Revival Hub, and other churches and production teams specifically request them. They're also the go-to mentors for everyone who comes after them: the folks teaching cables in week 1 are the same ones who learned it all in that very room.</p><figure class="production-photo"><img src="https://doop.design/photos/pexels/34623187.jpeg?h=900&w=1600" alt="Engineer working at an illuminated control desk" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Illustrative photography</figcaption></figure><p>That's the integration, plain and simple: PictureThis is the nonprofit behind the mission, the training, and the standards. Faithfire is its production arm, and its first success story. Every new cohort learns inside a real, working production company, not a simulation.</p></section></main><footer><p>Training: Faithfire Production, 139 Millwick Dr, Toronto.</p><p>PictureThis Production is being set up as a nonprofit organization in Ontario.</p><p>Faithfire Production is its production arm.</p><a href="/policies/">Our standards & policies</a> · <a href={"mailto:"+contactEmail}>{contactEmail}</a> · Placeholder contact</footer><script>document.querySelectorAll("header nav a").forEach(a=>{if(a.getAttribute("href")===location.pathname)a.setAttribute("aria-current","page")})</script></body></html>